WEBVTT

00:13.013 --> 00:15.598
LUCKY JERK

00:21.730 --> 00:22.689
Huh?

00:28.445 --> 00:29.863
Oh my!

00:31.948 --> 00:33.700
How cute!

00:33.783 --> 00:36.161
What's wrong? Are you all alone?

00:48.256 --> 00:50.425
Help me...

00:54.888 --> 00:56.556
This is the newspaper.

00:57.140 --> 00:58.308
Please look at this.

00:58.975 --> 01:03.313
Could this be the life-giving animal
En used to keep as a pet?

01:03.396 --> 01:06.524
So this is Chawantake?

01:06.608 --> 01:07.817
It's Kikurage.

01:07.901 --> 01:09.986
Good work. You may leave.

01:10.070 --> 01:11.112
If you'll excuse me!

01:12.072 --> 01:14.824
More people means
information comes in faster.

01:14.908 --> 01:18.078
Our organization is getting
bigger and bigger.

01:18.745 --> 01:19.913
Even now,

01:19.996 --> 01:23.625
workers are running at full capacity
to tattoo the crosses.

01:24.417 --> 01:26.878
What the hell are you doing, Natsuki?

01:27.921 --> 01:29.839
I thought smoke might come out.

01:29.923 --> 01:33.843
All right, Ton.
Go to that forest and investigate.

01:33.927 --> 01:35.095
Roger!

01:35.678 --> 01:39.641
If it's just Ton,
Kikurage might get scared and run away.

01:40.350 --> 01:41.976
Natsuki, you go too.

01:42.060 --> 01:43.478
What? Me too?

01:43.561 --> 01:47.357
I'm sure the boss wants
to obtain Kikurage's magic too.

01:47.899 --> 01:50.985
I'm concerned about that monster,
but I trust you.

01:51.569 --> 01:52.529
Yes, sir!

03:20.992 --> 03:22.911
THE BEGINNING

03:22.994 --> 03:24.412
PAYMENT

03:25.121 --> 03:26.623
This is the forest.

03:26.706 --> 03:30.168
The newspaper said it was near the stream.

03:35.006 --> 03:36.299
What's wrong, Natsuki?

03:36.382 --> 03:37.717
Well...

03:37.800 --> 03:41.763
It's about that smoke test
you did for me the other day.

03:41.846 --> 03:42.680
Yeah, and?

03:43.640 --> 03:46.684
For some reason,
you got some pretty good numbers.

03:46.768 --> 03:50.688
If it bugs you, I'll check it out
in detail when we get back.

03:51.439 --> 03:52.440
Please!

03:52.523 --> 03:56.027
I wanna be more useful to the boss!

03:56.110 --> 03:58.738
I'll get strong like you
and the others, Ton.

03:58.821 --> 04:01.908
It doesn't seem like
there's much you can do, though.

04:01.991 --> 04:03.451
Say what?

04:08.539 --> 04:12.210
Jeez, she keeps going through
all these narrow places.

04:13.419 --> 04:15.421
Wasn't there someone here just now?

04:16.214 --> 04:17.674
I've got a blister on my foot.

04:18.299 --> 04:21.844
With Kikurage's legs,
tailing her is a pain.

04:23.388 --> 04:25.598
This is the fourth day already.

04:25.682 --> 04:27.600
My heel is bleeding.

04:28.559 --> 04:31.980
But this is also for the sake
of reviving the En Family!

04:34.524 --> 04:36.484
FIVE DAYS AGO

04:40.154 --> 04:42.740
No way, the En mansion is...

04:42.824 --> 04:45.994
I can't believe
they took our mansion over.

04:46.661 --> 04:49.497
Are these the only ones who survived?

04:49.580 --> 04:52.166
What a bunch of half-dead losers.

04:53.751 --> 04:55.128
Thank you.

04:55.211 --> 04:58.506
We were able to escape the mansion
thanks to your magic.

04:59.340 --> 05:04.470
If it weren't for you,
we all would have been killed.

05:04.971 --> 05:08.433
I could have saved more people.

05:08.516 --> 05:09.726
I could have...

05:10.977 --> 05:14.355
You did more than enough.

05:14.439 --> 05:16.649
Mr. Turkey, who is this?

05:16.733 --> 05:19.027
You! Have you forgotten me?!

05:20.111 --> 05:21.446
Well...

05:21.529 --> 05:23.948
Fujita, that's rude of you.

05:24.032 --> 05:26.743
He's been a member
since the family was formed.

05:26.826 --> 05:28.328
His name is...

05:29.370 --> 05:32.749
His name is... I mean...

05:33.624 --> 05:34.792
That's enough.

05:38.046 --> 05:43.676
I also saved Shin and Noi when they were
about to be killed by the Cross-Eyes.

05:43.760 --> 05:48.181
At that time, I stole something
from the enemy without them knowing.

05:48.890 --> 05:50.683
Mr. En's severed head.

05:51.726 --> 05:54.437
That's great! You got it back.

05:54.520 --> 06:00.318
However, the Devil tumor in his head
had already been removed.

06:01.069 --> 06:04.322
No way! That means En is already...

06:04.405 --> 06:07.408
No, there's still hope.

06:07.492 --> 06:10.578
If we get Mr. En's Devil tumor
back from the Cross-Eyes,

06:10.661 --> 06:13.373
ask Noi to repair his body,

06:13.456 --> 06:15.416
and use Kikurage's magic...

06:15.500 --> 06:17.085
I see! But...

06:17.585 --> 06:20.505
But Kikurage is currently missing too.

06:20.588 --> 06:21.839
I see.

06:21.923 --> 06:25.510
That's where I come in again.

06:25.593 --> 06:26.803
Exactly.

06:26.886 --> 06:31.182
Fujita, can I leave
the search for Kikurage to you?

06:32.683 --> 06:34.602
I'll do it!

06:34.685 --> 06:37.480
I will definitely revive Mr. En!

06:39.107 --> 06:40.358
That's how it is.

06:40.942 --> 06:44.612
This is the Kikurage doll
that Mr. Turkey made.

06:44.695 --> 06:47.281
She moves so slowly, it's unbearable.

06:47.365 --> 06:49.117
This is so bad, I could puke.

06:49.200 --> 06:52.870
Ebisu! What the hell
did you come here for?!

06:52.954 --> 06:56.499
Snacks for Kikurage.

06:57.083 --> 07:01.796
That's it. You were closer
to Kikurage than me, right?

07:01.879 --> 07:05.883
All right. Once we find Kikurage,
I'll leave her to you.

07:07.802 --> 07:11.013
My stamina is at its limit.

07:16.018 --> 07:17.395
That is...

07:17.478 --> 07:20.189
It's Kikurage's voice! I'm sure of it!

07:20.273 --> 07:22.650
I'll contact Sho for now.

07:22.733 --> 07:25.653
- Kikurage, please be safe.
- Its butt!

07:28.364 --> 07:29.657
Kikurage.

07:30.241 --> 07:34.162
You don't need to be here anymore.

07:34.745 --> 07:36.914
I'm going to die soon.

07:39.000 --> 07:41.335
I'm sorry, En.

07:41.419 --> 07:44.297
You entrusted Kikurage to me,

07:44.380 --> 07:49.010
but I couldn't protect her until the end.

07:49.844 --> 07:51.554
I found her! That's Kikurage!

07:51.637 --> 07:53.055
There she is!

07:53.139 --> 07:56.684
The Cross-Eyes? Run, Kikurage! Run!

07:58.519 --> 08:00.438
Don't run away.

08:02.273 --> 08:04.442
I got her!

08:04.525 --> 08:07.153
You scumbags! Let go of Kikurage!

08:07.236 --> 08:10.656
How dare you kill my En? I'll kill you!

08:10.740 --> 08:12.867
You're Chota, right?

08:13.367 --> 08:16.162
Your name was on the list
of En family officers.

08:16.245 --> 08:19.832
Guess I'll take your head while I'm at it.

08:19.916 --> 08:21.209
You bastard!

08:21.292 --> 08:22.418
It's okay.

08:22.502 --> 08:25.463
I'll kill you in one shot
so you won't suffer.

08:25.546 --> 08:26.547
Ton!

08:26.631 --> 08:29.550
This is bad! There's another Kikurage.

08:29.634 --> 08:31.552
What?!

08:34.138 --> 08:36.557
To think we'd run into the Cross-Eyes...

08:37.350 --> 08:38.392
What now?

08:38.476 --> 08:40.978
At this rate, they'll kill both of them.

08:41.062 --> 08:45.566
On the other hand,
I'm not confident we can beat them.

08:51.739 --> 08:53.407
Ebisu?

08:59.163 --> 09:00.039
Whoa, what's this?

09:07.338 --> 09:09.590
- A monster?
- Natsuki!

09:17.557 --> 09:19.767
You're from the En family, I take it?

09:23.396 --> 09:25.523
Mr. Chota, are you okay?

09:25.606 --> 09:26.816
Fujita!

09:27.400 --> 09:29.652
Ebisu... What on earth is that?

09:29.735 --> 09:33.698
Surely, the Devil hairpin
that's still inside Ebisu's head

09:33.781 --> 09:36.117
and the emotions
stirred by Kikurage's crisis

09:36.200 --> 09:39.412
must have had
some kind of effect on her magic.

09:51.090 --> 09:52.758
What is that?

10:03.811 --> 10:05.896
Ebisu's magic isn't working?

10:05.980 --> 10:08.232
That's defense-type magic.

10:08.816 --> 10:12.028
I didn't know anyone in the Cross-Eyes
could use that kind of magic.

10:13.696 --> 10:15.489
Crap! She ran out of time!

10:15.573 --> 10:16.991
Ebisu!

10:17.074 --> 10:20.620
Fujita! Is everyone okay?!

10:24.457 --> 10:27.752
So this Kikurage was a fake.

10:27.835 --> 10:30.504
But Natsuki really surprised me.

10:31.380 --> 10:35.259
To think her smoke veins
would accidentally open from that cut.

10:35.343 --> 10:39.639
I'm sure you will be of use to the boss
with this magic.

10:39.722 --> 10:41.349
Natsuki.

10:44.477 --> 10:46.896
ADVANCED MAGIC

10:49.982 --> 10:51.400
FLOOD OF CUSTOMERS

10:51.484 --> 10:53.903
RECEPTION

10:56.113 --> 10:58.908
What is this place?

11:37.405 --> 11:38.989
Who are you?

11:41.701 --> 11:43.577
What is this place?

11:44.245 --> 11:45.955
You know, don't you?

11:49.417 --> 11:53.963
Shut up. I can't do anything about it!

11:54.630 --> 11:57.425
I don't plan to fight back!

12:12.189 --> 12:13.441
You're...

12:16.360 --> 12:17.194
Aikawa.

12:18.571 --> 12:19.905
Aikawa.

12:22.491 --> 12:25.953
Are you okay?
You were really moaning in your sleep.

12:26.036 --> 12:27.037
Yeah.

12:27.538 --> 12:30.583
So you have nightmares too?

12:37.298 --> 12:40.468
How are you, Risu?
How's your body feeling?

12:40.551 --> 12:42.970
I'm feeling much better now.

12:43.471 --> 12:47.224
I'm sorry you had to look after me
for two full days.

12:47.308 --> 12:48.559
Don't worry about it.

12:48.642 --> 12:51.187
Well, I'm off. I'll come back again.

12:51.687 --> 12:52.646
Aikawa.

12:53.856 --> 12:57.860
You're the only one
who cares about me this much.

12:58.444 --> 12:59.570
Thank you.

13:00.446 --> 13:04.116
That goes without saying.
We're partners. See you!

13:04.742 --> 13:06.869
You better get plenty of rest.

13:09.205 --> 13:12.124
TACHIKAWA APARTMENTS

13:14.293 --> 13:17.254
What was that place in my dream just now,

13:17.338 --> 13:20.674
and who was that man lighting a cigarette?

13:23.385 --> 13:26.806
Let's forget it.
I don't want to think about anything.

13:28.390 --> 13:33.854
I just want to live
a normal life as a Sorcerer.

13:34.355 --> 13:36.106
That's all I want,

13:37.566 --> 13:41.695
but maybe I shouldn't see Risu anymore.

13:43.239 --> 13:45.032
Another headache.

13:45.115 --> 13:47.535
Damn it. Crap.

13:48.160 --> 13:49.495
Damn it!

13:58.420 --> 14:00.548
Put some oil on me, Hayes.

14:00.631 --> 14:01.799
Okay.

14:02.550 --> 14:06.554
Haru, is there any point in doing this?
You're a Devil.

14:06.637 --> 14:08.556
It's for the mood. The mood.

14:13.686 --> 14:15.062
Good job.

14:18.148 --> 14:23.821
Hayes. I've thought this for a while,
but that look isn't my taste.

14:23.904 --> 14:24.780
What?

14:24.864 --> 14:27.199
Doesn't it make us look
like mother and son?

14:27.283 --> 14:28.951
Devil power!

14:32.872 --> 14:33.706
What?

14:33.789 --> 14:36.709
You turned me into an adult in an instant!

14:37.501 --> 14:40.087
Even the glasses appeared out of nowhere.

14:40.170 --> 14:46.302
Everything you do breaks apart
the scientist I've been my whole life.

14:47.344 --> 14:48.846
What do you say, Hayes?

14:50.723 --> 14:53.893
Why don't you come live with me in Hell?

14:53.976 --> 14:57.396
It's better than being
in that garbage dump Hole, right?

14:58.981 --> 15:02.151
A choice between Hell and the Hole.

15:02.234 --> 15:03.611
That's a tough call.

15:04.862 --> 15:09.283
You're mine! Do as I say, human!

15:09.366 --> 15:13.287
- Don't suddenly flip your appearance!
- That was close. I nearly died.

15:14.580 --> 15:19.793
Anyway, like I've been saying all along,
I want to find Ai.

15:19.877 --> 15:23.130
Is it really that important to you?

15:23.213 --> 15:25.090
Of course it's important.

15:25.174 --> 15:30.554
Whether it's possible to turn a human
into a Sorcerer through science

15:30.638 --> 15:33.057
is hugely important to my research.

15:33.140 --> 15:36.602
Okay, I get it. I'll help you find him.

15:36.685 --> 15:38.270
Thank you, Haru!

15:38.354 --> 15:41.732
More importantly, can you change me back?

15:41.815 --> 15:43.651
I feel weird in a lot of ways.

15:43.734 --> 15:45.486
What?

15:49.156 --> 15:51.909
- Package for you.
- Thank you.

15:52.409 --> 15:54.745
I'm glad it arrived safely.

15:54.828 --> 15:55.746
Now, then...

16:06.632 --> 16:08.008
What a surprise.

16:08.092 --> 16:12.179
This suit is twice the weight
they use in a normal Devil test,

16:12.262 --> 16:14.515
but it handles the work without trouble.

16:19.103 --> 16:20.854
Next is the rinse!

16:20.938 --> 16:22.523
Nikaido!

16:22.606 --> 16:24.733
Shall we eat?

16:28.737 --> 16:32.783
Okay, eat my special Devil-meat dish
today as well.

16:33.492 --> 16:35.703
Devil meat again today?

16:35.786 --> 16:37.955
This is also part of your training.

16:38.497 --> 16:41.417
Could this meat be...

16:41.500 --> 16:45.004
It may look bad, but it tastes great.

16:46.130 --> 16:51.760
Asu, isn't what I'm doing
the training for the Devil exam?

16:52.261 --> 16:55.431
But I don't intend to become a Devil.

16:55.514 --> 17:00.519
I thought that if you failed using magic
when you were young,

17:00.602 --> 17:05.149
it would be better for you
to first train to produce a lot of smoke.

17:05.232 --> 17:09.570
The training for the Devil exam
happens to be perfect for that.

17:09.653 --> 17:10.821
Really?

17:11.905 --> 17:16.160
Well then, try to produce
as much smoke as you can.

17:16.243 --> 17:17.161
Okay.

17:25.627 --> 17:27.129
Don't be afraid.

17:27.629 --> 17:30.632
I'm pretty sure you failed
when you were little

17:30.716 --> 17:33.385
because you didn't produce enough smoke.

17:33.469 --> 17:34.303
Asu...

17:38.932 --> 17:39.808
All right.

17:52.488 --> 17:54.073
Don't look away!

17:54.156 --> 17:56.408
Keep producing smoke!

18:03.749 --> 18:07.252
The shape of the cube changed!

18:08.003 --> 18:12.508
Nikaido, produce more smoke!
I'm sure it'll keep changing!

18:14.093 --> 18:17.596
I can't keep doing it anymore.

18:21.850 --> 18:23.018
Nikaido!

18:25.604 --> 18:26.814
LIBRARY - CAFETERIA

18:26.897 --> 18:29.691
Stop right there, Aikawa!

18:30.692 --> 18:31.527
Whoa!

18:34.029 --> 18:37.032
Give back the school lunch ingredients,
you scumbag!

18:37.116 --> 18:39.785
Damn it, I'm cornered.

18:39.868 --> 18:43.539
If you come any closer,
I may fall from here and die.

18:43.622 --> 18:45.541
Isn't that a great idea?

18:45.624 --> 18:46.792
Just die!

18:46.875 --> 18:49.044
Smash your brains against the ground.

18:49.128 --> 18:50.295
How awful of you!

18:51.088 --> 18:51.922
Shit!

18:52.005 --> 18:53.132
Aikawa?!

18:53.215 --> 18:55.342
Just kidding!

18:55.425 --> 18:56.593
Whoa!

18:57.845 --> 18:59.638
See you!

19:09.898 --> 19:14.528
He comes to school,
eats, plays, and sleeps.

19:14.611 --> 19:17.072
He's the same Aikawa I know.

19:18.282 --> 19:22.578
I can't believe
he would tell someone about my magic,

19:22.661 --> 19:25.664
especially not someone
from the Cross-Eyes.

19:26.832 --> 19:29.251
Huh? Isn't that you, Risu?

19:29.334 --> 19:31.336
- Quiet!
- It's been a while!

19:31.420 --> 19:32.588
Risu?

19:36.175 --> 19:39.595
If you came to school,
you should have talked to me.

19:43.140 --> 19:46.727
You're full of mysteries.

19:48.145 --> 19:50.105
Mysteries? Like what?

19:50.772 --> 19:56.361
Like where you live
or where you make money to eat.

19:56.445 --> 19:57.362
Everything!

19:59.448 --> 20:03.619
You haven't even told me
what your magic is.

20:03.702 --> 20:06.955
Even though
I haven't hidden anything from you.

20:07.039 --> 20:11.627
Risu. Like I told you,
I can only produce a little bit of smoke.

20:11.710 --> 20:13.378
Don't play dumb!

20:13.462 --> 20:16.590
You're the only one
I've told about my magic.

20:16.673 --> 20:22.137
You told someone about my magic,
and I got killed for it!

20:22.221 --> 20:24.890
It's not like that, Risu.
Listen to me. I--

20:24.973 --> 20:27.768
There's no way
I can believe anything you say!

20:29.353 --> 20:33.148
I'll make the Cross-Eyes
tell me the truth directly.

20:33.232 --> 20:35.400
I've got the power for it now.

20:35.484 --> 20:37.402
Risu! Hey, wait!

20:39.029 --> 20:42.491
Could he be heading to En's mansion?

20:48.497 --> 20:50.707
Sorry for making you push yourself.

20:50.791 --> 20:53.210
It's fine. But I was surprised.

20:53.293 --> 20:55.712
I never thought the cube would transform.

20:56.213 --> 21:01.093
However, what should I do
to master my magic?

21:04.346 --> 21:08.934
Actually, I've read about a case
similar to your magic in a book.

21:10.060 --> 21:12.145
But it was a long time ago.

21:12.896 --> 21:15.941
If only I could
read that book again somehow.

21:17.401 --> 21:19.194
Where is that book now?

21:19.278 --> 21:21.697
It's a book written in Devil language.

21:21.780 --> 21:25.075
En should be the only Sorcerer who has it.

21:25.158 --> 21:26.785
En's mansion, right?

21:27.369 --> 21:29.121
Okay, let's go!

21:30.414 --> 21:33.542
Currently, the Cross-Eyes
are occupying the mansion.

21:34.042 --> 21:35.544
It's very dangerous.

21:35.627 --> 21:41.008
Moreover, there's a good chance
you've been flagged as En's partner.

21:41.800 --> 21:47.097
To look for the small book
inside the mansion, we'll need a disguise.

21:47.180 --> 21:48.390
A disguise?

21:48.473 --> 21:50.851
Okay, let's use this.

21:52.436 --> 21:53.812
Take off your clothes,

21:53.895 --> 21:57.983
set the bottles in the machine
in this room, and pull the lever.

21:58.066 --> 21:59.484
All right.

22:00.068 --> 22:04.031
Oh, man.
I can finally take off this armor.

22:05.365 --> 22:08.493
The clothes to wear
after transforming are inside?

22:08.577 --> 22:11.747
At last,
I might get to wear decent clothes.

22:12.748 --> 22:14.499
Let's see...

22:15.292 --> 22:18.712
Set the bottles here and here

22:18.795 --> 22:20.714
and pull the lever.

22:21.298 --> 22:22.466
OCCUPIED

24:20.709 --> 24:21.918
THE END

24:22.002 --> 24:24.212
What we learned in Episode 10.

24:24.296 --> 24:26.173
Sho saved the En family.

24:26.256 --> 24:28.133
Natsuki's magic repels everything.

24:28.216 --> 24:30.469
Nikaido's magic is undeveloped.

24:30.552 --> 24:34.598
What we'll learn in Episode 11
is still hidden in chaos.

24:34.681 --> 24:36.933
This is Dorohedoro.
